From: Eric MacDonald <eric.macdonald@windriver.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:41:56 +0000
Subject: Fix duplicate EFI $INSTBR boot entries not deleted on reinstall

The installer performs a pre-create cleanup of existing EFI boot
entries matching ${INSTBR} (e.g. "starlingx") before creating the
new boot entry.

There are two issues with the existing cleanup.

First, the match assumes the efibootmgr output ends immediately after
the boot entry label:

grep "^Boot.*\* ${INSTBR}$"

However, the new version of efibootmgr output includes the EFI device
path after the label ; like this:

Boot000#* starlingx     HD(2,GPT,...)/File(\EFI\BOOT\bootx64.efi)

Where the previous version was:

Boot000#* starlingx

The '$' end-of-line anchor therefore prevents these entries from
matching, leaving stale ${INSTBR} entries behind across reinstalls.

Second, if multiple matching boot numbers are returned, the previous
code passes the newline-separated value to a single command:

efibootmgr -b ${oldboonum} -B

The -b option accepts a single boot number, so only one entry can be
deleted per invocation and the remaining values are not processed as
separate boot entries.

Replace the grep/sed expression with a sed match that accounts for the
whitespace and device path following ${INSTBR} and extracts only the
EFI boot number.

Then loop over all matching boot numbers and issue a separate:

efibootmgr -b <num> -B

for each entry.

This ensures all stale ${INSTBR} EFI boot entries are removed before
the new entry is created, preventing duplicate boot entries from
accumulating across reinstalls.

Signed-off-by: Eric MacDonald <eric.macdonald@windriver.com>
---
 init-ostree-install.sh | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/init-ostree-install.sh b/init-ostree-install.sh
index 83a7509..8266eff 100644
--- a/init-ostree-install.sh
+++ b/init-ostree-install.sh
@@ -1720,9 +1720,20 @@ fi
 if [ -d /sys/firmware/efi/efivars ] ;then
     if which efibootmgr >/dev/null 2>&1; then
         mount -t efivarfs efivarfs /sys/firmware/efi/efivars
-        oldboonum=`efibootmgr | grep "^Boot.*\* ${INSTBR}$" |sed "s/Boot\(.*\)\* ${INSTBR}/\1/g"`
-        if [ -n "${oldboonum}" ]; then
-            efibootmgr -b ${oldboonum} -B
+        log_info "searching for and removing old boot entries for ${INSTBR}"
+        oldbootnums=$(efibootmgr | sed -n "s/^Boot\([0-9A-Fa-f]*\)\* ${INSTBR}[[:space:]].*/\1/p")
+        if [ -n "${oldbootnums}" ]; then
+            for b in ${oldbootnums}; do
+                efibootmgr -b "${b}" -B >/dev/null 2>&1
+                rc=$?
+                if [ $rc -eq 0 ]; then
+                    log_info "... successfully deleted boot entry ${b}"
+                else
+                    log_error "... failed to delete boot entry ${b}, exit code ${rc}"
+                fi
+            done
+        else
+            log_info "... no existing boot entries found for ${INSTBR}"
         fi
         if [ "$EFIBOOT_FIRST" = "1" ]; then
             efibootmgr -b 0 -B >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
